  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1155 PM CDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nFriday through Monday:\n\nBreezy northerly winds will develop Friday in the wake of the\ncold front. The wind speeds will depend on the amplitude of the\nassociated upper trough. Then high pressure will slide across\nthe Great Lakes from Friday night through Saturday afternoon.\nAnother upper trough will swing across Lake Superior Saturday\nnight, but it looks like any rain will miss southern WI at this\ntime. High pressure will return Sunday through Tuesday.\nHighs will be in the lower to mid 60s, with lows in the 40s. \n\nCronce",
